## Why This Is Asked

This evaluates the ability to design a plugin-friendly, runtime-extensible load balancing system for edge proxies, focusing on decoupling and safe dynamic strategy selection.

## Key Concepts

- Strategy pattern for algorithm abstraction
- Registry-based plugin architecture
- Runtime extensibility without core modifications
- State management for routing decisions
- Isolated testing of individual strategies

## Code Example

```javascript
interface LoadBalancingStrategy {
  selectPeer(route: any, peers: string[], state: any): string;
}

class Registry {
  private map = new Map<string, LoadBalancingStrategy>();

  register(name: string, strategy: LoadBalancingStrategy) {
    this.map.set(name, strategy);
  }

  get(name: string): LoadBalancingStrategy {
    return this.map.get(name);
  }
}

// Example usage
class RoundRobinStrategy implements LoadBalancingStrategy {
  selectPeer(route: any, peers: string[], state: any): string {
    const index = state[route.id] || 0;
    state[route.id] = (index + 1) % peers.length;
    return peers[index];
  }
}

const registry = new Registry();
registry.register('round_robin', new RoundRobinStrategy());
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests the ability to design a small, extensible plugin system for logging using runtime registration and fault isolation.

## Key Concepts
- **Open-Closed Principle**: The Logger remains open for extension but closed for modification
- **Strategy/Plugin Patterns**: Each backend implements a common interface and can be swapped or added at runtime
- **Registry Pattern**: Enables runtime backend discovery and management by name
- **Asynchronous Dispatch**: Non-blocking logging ensures performance isn't impacted by slow backends
- **Fault Isolation**: A failing backend shouldn't crash the entire application

## Code Example
```typescript
interface Backend {
  name: string;
  log(level: LogLevel, msg: string, meta?: Record<string, unknown>): void | Promise<void>;
}

type LogLevel = 'debug' | 'info' | 'warn' | 'error';

class BackendRegistry {
  private backends = new Map<string, Backend>();

  register(name: string, backend: Backend): void {
    this.backends.set(name, backend);
  }

  get(name: string): Backend | undefined {
    return this.backends.get(name);
  }

  unregister(name: string): boolean {
    return this.backends.delete(name);
  }
}

class Logger {
  constructor(private registry: BackendRegistry) {}

  async log(level: LogLevel, msg: string, meta?: Record<string, unknown>): Promise<void> {
    const backends = Array.from(this.registry['backends'].values());
    await Promise.allSettled(
      backends.map(backend =>
        Promise.resolve(backend.log(level, msg, meta)).catch(() => {})
      )
    );
  }

  debug(msg: string, meta?: Record<string, unknown>): Promise<void> {
    return this.log('debug', msg, meta);
  }

  info(msg: string, meta?: Record<string, unknown>): Promise<void> {
    return this.log('info', msg, meta);
  }

  warn(msg: string, meta?: Record<string, unknown>): Promise<void> {
    return this.log('warn', msg, meta);
  }

  error(msg: string, meta?: Record<string, unknown>): Promise<void> {
    return this.log('error', msg, meta);
  }
}

// Usage Example
const registry = new BackendRegistry();

const consoleBackend: Backend = {
  name: 'console',
  log(level, msg, meta) {
    console.log(`[${level}] ${msg}`, meta || '');
  },
};

const fileBackend: Backend = {
  name: 'file',
  async log(level, msg, meta) {
    // Write to file implementation
  },
};

registry.register('console', consoleBackend);
registry.register('file', fileBackend);

const logger = new Logger(registry);
logger.info('Application started', { version: '1.0.0' });
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests runtime extensibility and correctness of flag evaluation, including versioning and thread-safety.

## Key Concepts
- Strategy pattern for evaluation logic
- Registry/Factory for runtime additions
- Thread-safety and version-keying
- Performance implications of dynamic dispatch

## Code Example
```typescript
interface User { id: string; segments: string[]; }
interface Flag { name: string; version: string; defaultValue?: boolean; }

interface FlagEvaluationStrategy {
  evaluate(user: User, flag: Flag): boolean;
}
type StrategyFactory = () => FlagEvaluationStrategy;

class FlagRegistry {
  private map = new Map<string, StrategyFactory>();
  register(key: string, factory: StrategyFactory) { this.map.set(key, factory); }
  get(key: string): FlagEvaluationStrategy {
    const f = this.map.get(key);
    if (!f) throw new Error(`No strategy registered for ${key}`);
    return f();
  }
}
class FlagEvaluator {
  constructor(private registry: FlagRegistry) {}
  eval(flag: Flag, user: User): boolean {
    const strat = this.registry.get(`${flag.name}|${flag.version}`);
    return strat.evaluate(user, flag);
  }
}
class PercentStrategy implements FlagEvaluationStrategy {
  constructor(private percent: number) {}
  evaluate(user: User, flag: Flag): boolean {
    const r = (parseInt(user.id.slice(-4), 10) % 100) < this.percent;
    return r;
  }
}
```

